(vector (map (:db/id -1)
  (:adr/doc_type "adr")
  (:adr/id "adr-2609111400-a-repository-that-answers-25-is-worth-more-than-nine-that-answer-30")
  (:adr/topic "q9-parity-harness-coverage")
  (:adr/title "A repository that answers 25 is worth more than nine that answer 30")
  (:adr/status "accepted")
  (:adr/date "2026-09-11")
  (:adr/deciders (vector "Jun Kawasaki" "Claude Opus 5"))
  (:adr/repos (vector "com-junkawasaki/root" "kotoba-lang/com-adyen"))
  (:adr/related (vector "adr-2609111300-eight-of-twenty-pilots-now-have-a-parity-harness"))
  (:adr/body
  "## Context

Second batch of generated parity harnesses, same procedure as the first:
generate, `amu check`, compile to aarch64-macos, execute through
`tools/kexe_loader.c`, compare selector by selector, and only then land.
Coverage moves from eight to eleven of twenty.

`com-acorrd-standards`, `com-acquia` and `com-adyen`. The third was picked
deliberately.

## Why com-adyen was the one to include

Every parity run so far has reported the same route count: 30. A number that is
identical everywhere is exactly the kind of agreement that cannot be read --
it agrees with a correct derivation, and equally with a constant that was
hard-coded on both sides and never depended on anything.

`com-adyen` declares FIVE entities rather than six, and both sides answer 25.

    com-acorrd-standards   native 30   oracle 30
    com-acquia             native 30   oracle 30
    com-adyen              native 25   oracle 25

That single 25 is what makes the nine 30s informative. It shows the count is
computed from the entity table on the ARTIFACT side too, not just in the
harness, so the agreements elsewhere are evidence about a derivation rather
than a coincidence of constants.

The general form is the one this cohort keeps running into from different
directions: a measurement that only ever produces one value has not
demonstrated that it can produce another.

## It also separates two generators

The COMPONENT generator refuses `com-adyen`: no spec declares a ref, so no
expand oracle can be derived (adr-2609111100). The HARNESS generator does not
care -- it needs `routes`, `as-int`, `as-bool` and `page-limit`, and refs are
not among them. Confirmed by running it: the harness generated, compiled and
verified normally.

Worth recording because the two refusals could easily be assumed to travel
together, and they do not.

## Result

All three: `amu check :ok true`, compiled, executed.

    route count   agrees on both sides (30, 30, 25)
    as-bool       9 of 9
    page-limit    8 of 8
    as-int        5 of 6, the \"12abc\" row differing

The ninth, tenth and eleventh reproductions of the cohort reader-conditional
divergence, and in each run the only differing row -- so a run in which
everything matched would be a reason to suspect the harness never reached the
artifact, not a better result.

## Still not covered

Eleven of twenty is coverage of FOUR layers, not of the components. The store,
filter, pagination, handler and expand layers need fixtures shaped to each
repository's entities and are not generated. Nine pilots have no harness at
all.")))
